<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · ReloadAlert"
  description="Privacy Policy for ReloadAlert, the Safari extension for Mac that reloads tabs and alerts you when a page changes."
  eyebrow="ReloadAlert"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  meta="Last updated: October 29, 2026"
  back={{ href: '/apps/auto-refresh', label: 'ReloadAlert' }}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> ReloadAlert collects no data. Everything it keeps stays in Safari on your Mac, and nothing is sent to us or anyone else.
  </div>

  <h2>What It Collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The extension makes no network requests of its own; it only reloads the tabs you choose.
  </p>

  <h2>What Stays on Your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your settings</strong> for each tab (interval, keywords, the element you picked) are stored locally in Safari and cleared when you close the tab.</li>
    <li><strong>Watched pages.</strong> To notice a change, the extension reads the text of pages you chose to watch and compares it on your Mac. It keeps only a short excerpt and a fingerprint (hash) of that text, locally in Safari, so the next reload can be compared. Both are deleted when you close the tab.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Access to websites (to reload and watch the tabs you turn on), tabs, local storage, and messaging with the ReloadAlert app on your Mac, used only to show a Mac notification.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com">matt@mattdonders.com</a></p>
</DocLayout>
